.&lt;/text&gt;</markedFeedback_xml><showPrefix>true</showPrefix><prefixActivityLevel>false</prefixActivityLevel><prefixStartIndex /><showPrefixes>false</showPrefixes><blankMinWidth>200</blankMinWidth><blankMaxWidth>650</blankMaxWidth><question_xml><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>true</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>true</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>He agreed [to be photographed] wearing a wig of long blonde hair. (&lt;i&gt;photograph&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/2321.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>He agreed &lt;b&gt;to be photographed&lt;/b&gt; wearing a wig of long blonde hair.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>true</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>true</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>I can vividly recall [being told] I was stupid by my first teacher at school. (&lt;i&gt;tell&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/2322.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>I can vividly recall &lt;b&gt;being told&lt;/b&gt; I was stupid by my first teacher at school.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>true</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>true</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>They said they resented [being called] terrorists and were in fact freedom fighters. (&lt;i&gt;call&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/2323.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>They said they resented &lt;b&gt;being called&lt;/b&gt; terrorists and were in fact freedom fighters.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>true</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>true</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>The woman who accused the boys refused [to be named] by the media for fear of reprisals. (&lt;i&gt;name&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/2324.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>The woman who accused the boys refused &lt;b&gt;to be named&lt;/b&gt; by the media for fear of reprisals.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>I remember [being given] this ring by my grandmother when I was six years old. (&lt;i&gt;give&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/2325.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>I remember &lt;b&gt;being given&lt;/b&gt; this ring by my grandmother when I was six years old.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>She wrote a book on Italian cooking and came [to be seen] as an expert on the subject. (&lt;i&gt;see&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/2326.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>She wrote a book on Italian cooking and came &lt;b&gt;to be seen&lt;/b&gt; as an expert on the subject.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>The referee appeared [to be hit] by a bottle thrown from the crowd. (&lt;i&gt;hit&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/2327.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>The referee appeared &lt;b&gt;to be hit&lt;/b&gt; by a bottle thrown from the crowd.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>Thousands of students face [being turned away] from university this year because of a shortage of places. (&lt;i&gt;turn away&lt;/I&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/2328.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>Thousands of students face &lt;b&gt;being turned away&lt;/b&gt; from university this year because of a shortage of places. </modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>All three of the men denied [being involved] in the robbery. (&lt;i&gt;involve&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/2329.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>All three of the men denied &lt;b&gt;being involved&lt;/b&gt; in the robbery.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>I hope [to be posted] to a school on the east coast, but there’s no guarantee of it. (&lt;i&gt;post&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/23210.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>I hope &lt;b&gt;to be posted&lt;/b&gt; to a school on the east coast, but there’s no guarantee of it.</modelAnswerString></question></question_xml><enableAudioOnChecked>false</enab